From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: preserve LLVM allocation metadata with GCC

DXC's older LLVM writes User allocation flags before construction and reads
them after destruction. GCC lifetime-based dead-store elimination can remove
these writes, causing DXIL compilation to free the wrong pointer. The failure
reproduces in DxilValueCache's PHINode sentinel destructor with GCC 16 and LTO.

Backport the compiler-flag workaround from LLVM 18's HandleLLVMOptions.cmake,
using DXC's older add_flag_if_supported signature. Unsupported compilers do not
receive this flag. Keep the distribution's optimization and target flags.

References: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/57740
            https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/llvmorg-18.1.8/llvm/cmake/modules/HandleLLVMOptions.cmake

--- a/cmake/modules/HandleLLVMOptions.cmake
+++ b/cmake/modules/HandleLLVMOptions.cmake
@@ -502,6 +502,12 @@
     add_flag_if_supported("-Werror=date-time" WERROR_DATE_TIME)
   endif ()
 
+  # User allocation metadata must survive construction and destruction.
+  # GCC lifetime-based DSE otherwise removes these writes, notably with LTO.
+  # Match the workaround used by LLVM before its allocation code was fixed.
+  # Probe the flag so other compilers retain their existing behavior.
+  add_flag_if_supported("-fno-lifetime-dse" NO_LIFETIME_DSE)
+
   if (LLVM_ENABLE_MODULES)
     set(OLD_CMAKE_REQUIRED_FLAGS ${CMAKE_REQUIRED_FLAGS})
     set(CMAKE_REQUIRED_FLAGS "${CMAKE_REQUIRED_FLAGS} -fmodules -fcxx-modules")
